    }
   },
   "clip": "../09_Animation/SC009.mp4",
   "audio": "../10_Audio/narration/SC009.wav"
  },
  {
   "id": 10,
   "file": "SC010",
   "section": "Meet the cleanup crew",
   "start": 62.833,
   "duration": 7.708,
   "narration": "Vultures are big, broad-winged birds built for one job: finding dead animals, and finishing them fast.",
   "visual": {
    "type": "plate",
    "shot": "P10",
    "move": "pan_l"
   },
   "clip": "../09_Animation/SC010.mp4",
   "audio": "../10_Audio/narration/SC010.wav"
  },
  {
   "id": 11,
   "file": "SC011",
   "section": "Meet the cleanup crew",
   "start": 70.541,
   "duration": 8.042,
   "narration": "They barely flap. They ride columns of rising warm air, circling for hours while they scan the ground below.",
   "visual": {
    "type": "card",
    "card": "thermal"
   },
   "clip": "../09_Animation/SC011.mp4",
   "audio": "../10_Audio/narration/SC011.wav"
  },
  {
   "id": 12,
   "file": "SC012",
   "section": "Meet the cleanup crew",
   "start": 78.583,
   "duration": 11.333,
   "narration": "They also watch each other. When one vulture drops toward a carcass, others see it and follow, so a single meal can pull in birds from kilometres around.",
   "visual": {
    "type": "plate",
    "shot": "P01",
    "move": "pull"
   },
   "clip": "../09_Animation/SC012.mp4",
   "audio": "../10_Audio/narration/SC012.wav"
  },
  {
   "id": 13,
   "file": "SC013",
   "section": "Meet the cleanup crew",
   "start": 89.916,
   "duration": 8.167,
   "narration": "One R\u00fcppell's vulture was hit by a plane at eleven thousand three hundred metres. That's higher than Mount Everest.",
   "visual": {
    "type": "plate",
    "shot": "P11",
    "move": "push",
    "text": {
     "style": "callout",
     "main": "11,300 m",
     "sub": "R\u00fcppell's vulture \u00b7 1973"
    }
   },
   "clip": "../09_Animation/SC013.mp4",
   "audio": "../10_Audio/narration/SC013.wav"
  },
  {
   "id": 14,
   "file": "SC014",
   "section": "Meet the cleanup crew",
   "start": 98.083,
   "duration": 8.542,
   "narration": "That bald head isn't a flaw. Bare skin stays cleaner when you feed inside a carcass, and it may help the bird shed heat.",
   "visual": {
    "type": "plate",
    "shot": "P14",
    "move": "push",
    "tag": "HYPOTHESIS"
   },
   "clip": "../09_Animation/SC014.mp4",
   "audio": "../10_Audio/narration/SC014.wav"
  },
  {
   "id": 15,
   "file": "SC015",
   "section": "Meet the cleanup crew",
   "start": 106.625,
   "duration": 11.333,
   "narration": "And their stomachs are brutal. Harsh acid and specialised gut bacteria let them eat meat carrying germs like anthrax, which would sicken most other animals.",
   "visual": {
    "type": "card",
    "card": "gut",
    "tag": "STRONG"
   },
   "clip": "../09_Animation/SC015.mp4",
   "audio": "../10_Audio/narration/SC015.wav"
  },
  {
   "id": 16,
   "file": "SC016",
   "section": "Meet the cleanup crew",
   "start": 117.958,
   "duration": 6.75,
   "narration": "In other words, a vulture isn't just eating garbage. It's taking disease out of circulation.",
   "visual": {
    "type": "plate",
    "shot": "P02",
    "move": "pull",
    "fx": [
     "dust"
    ]
   },
   "clip": "../09_Animation/SC016.mp4",
   "audio": "../10_Audio/narration/SC016.wav"
  },
  {
   "id": 17,
   "file": "SC017",
   "section": "The collapse",
   "start": 124.708,
   "duration": 8.333,
   "narration": "In India, vultures were part of everyday life: on rooftops, on old trees, circling over every town dump.",
   "visual": {
    "type": "plate",
    "shot": "P15",
    "move": "push",
    "text": {
     "style": "chapter",
     "main": "THE COLLAPSE",
     "sub": "Chapter 2"
    }
   },
   "clip": "../09_Animation/SC017.mp4",
   "audio": "../10_Audio/narration/SC017.wav"
  },
  {
   "id": 18,
   "file": "SC018",
   "section": "The collapse",
   "start": 133.041,
   "duration": 9.167,
   "narration": "Then, through the 1990s, birdwatchers started noticing empty nests, and dead vultures lying under their roosts.",
   "visual": {
    "type": "plate",
    "shot": "P17",
    "move": "push"
   },
   "clip": "../09_Animation/SC018.mp4",
   "audio": "../10_Audio/narration/SC018.wav"
  },
  {
   "id": 19,
   "file": "SC019",
   "section": "The collapse",
   "start": 142.208,
   "duration": 9.167,
   "narration": "Surveys showed losses of more than ninety-five percent. For the white-rumped vulture, by some estimates, ninety-nine point nine.",
   "visual": {
    "type": "card",
    "card": "decline",
    "tag": "STRONG"
   },
   "clip": "../09_Animation/SC019.mp4",
   "audio": "../10_Audio/narration/SC019.wav"
  },
  {
   "id": 20,
   "file": "SC020",
   "section": "The collapse",
   "start": 151.375,
   "duration": 5.375,
   "narration": "Scientists suspected a virus. Pesticides. Something in the water.",
   "visual": {
    "type": "card",
    "card": "suspects"
   },
   "clip": "../09_Animation/SC020.mp4",
   "audio": "../10_Audio/narration/SC020.wav"
  },
  {
   "id": 21,
   "file": "SC021",
   "section": "The collapse",
   "start": 156.75,
   "duration": 4.875,
   "narration": "The real killer was hiding in plain sight, in a medicine cabinet.",
   "visual": {
    "type": "plate",
    "shot": "P16",
    "move": "push"
   },
   "clip": "../09_Animation/SC021.mp4",
   "audio": "../10_Audio/narration/SC021.wav"
  },
  {
   "id": 22,
   "file": "SC022",
   "section": "The collapse",
   "start": 161.625,
   "duration": 5.708,
   "narration": "Diclofenac: a cheap painkiller that farmers gave to sick and injured cattle.",
   "visual": {
    "type": "plate",
    "shot": "P19",
    "move": "pan_r",
    "text": {
     "style": "label",
     "main": "DICLOFENAC",
     "sub": "veterinary painkiller"
    }
   },
   "clip": "../09_Animation/SC022.mp4",
   "audio": "../10_Audio/narration/SC022.wav"
  },
  {
   "id": 23,
   "file": "SC023",
   "section": "The collapse",
   "start": 167.333,
   "duration": 7.958,
   "narration": "When a treated cow died, traces of the drug stayed in its body. Harmless to the cow. Deadly to a vulture.",
   "visual": {
    "type": "card",
    "card": "chain",
    "tag": "STRONG"
   },
   "clip": "../09_Animation/SC023.mp4",
   "audio": "../10_Audio/narration/SC023.wav"
  },
  {
   "id": 24,
   "file": "SC024",
   "section": "The collapse",
   "start": 175.291,
   "duration": 7.708,
   "narration": "Their kidneys failed within days, and a single contaminated carcass could poison dozens of birds at once.",
   "visual": {
    "type": "plate",
    "shot": "P17",
    "move": "pull"
   },
   "clip": "../09_Animation/SC024.mp4",
   "audio": "../10_Audio/narration/SC024.wav"
  },
  {
   "id": 25,
   "file": "SC025",
   "section": "The collapse",
   "start": 182.999,
   "duration": 10.667,
   "narration": "And it took shockingly little. One study calculated that if fewer than one carcass in a hundred carried a lethal dose, that alone could explain the crash.",
   "visual": {
    "type": "card",
    "card": "grid",
    "tag": "STRONG"
   },
   "clip": "../09_Animation/SC025.mp4",
   "audio": "../10_Audio/narration/SC025.wav"
  },
  {
   "id": 26,
   "file": "SC026",
   "section": "The collapse",
   "start": 193.666,
   "duration": 6.125,
   "narration": "Today, three of South Asia's vulture species are listed as critically endangered.",
   "visual": {
    "type": "card",
    "card": "redlist",
    "tag": "STRONG"
   },
   "clip": "../09_Animation/SC026.mp4",
   "audio": "../10_Audio/narration/SC026.wav"
  },
  {
   "id": 27,
   "file": "SC027",
   "section": "The collapse",
   "start": 199.791,
   "duration": 8.708,
   "narration": "In 2004, researchers finally proved the link. India banned veterinary diclofenac in 2006.",
   "visual": {
    "type": "card",
    "card": "timeline",
    "items": [
     [
      "2004",
      "Cause proven"
     ],
     [
      "2006",
      "India bans vet diclofenac"
     ]
    ],
    "tag": "STRONG"
   },
   "clip": "../09_Animation/SC027.mp4",
   "audio": "../10_Audio/narration/SC027.wav"
  },
  {
   "id": 28,
   "file": "SC028",
   "section": "The collapse",
   "start": 208.499,
   "duration": 4.792,
   "narration": "But by then, the sky above India was already almost empty.",
   "visual": {
    "type": "plate",
    "shot": "P12",
    "move": "sink"
   },
   "clip": "../09_Animation/SC028.mp4",
   "audio": "../10_Audio/narration/SC028.wav"
  },
  {
   "id": 29,
   "file": "SC029",
   "section": "A world without vultures",
   "start": 213.291,
   "duration": 8.292,
   "narration": "So let's go back to that cow at the edge of the village. Same place. Same morning. But this time, no vultures come.",
   "visual": {
    "type": "plate",
    "shot": "P03",
    "move": "push",
    "tab": "DAY 1 \u00b7 No vultures",
