   "section": "A world without vultures",
   "start": 232.541,
   "duration": 13.833,
   "narration": "This part has been tested. In a 2025 experiment in Costa Rica, carcasses that vultures couldn't reach took about twice as long to break down, and drew nearly twice as many flies.",
   "visual": {
    "type": "card",
    "card": "compare",
    "title": "Costa Rica, 2025",
    "rows": [
     [
      "Time to decompose",
      "\u00d72"
     ],
     [
      "Flies at carcass",
      "\u00d72"
     ]
    ],
    "tag": "STRONG"
   },
   "clip": "../09_Animation/SC032.mp4",
   "audio": "../10_Audio/narration/SC032.wav"
  },
  {
   "id": 33,
   "file": "SC033",
   "section": "A world without vultures",
   "start": 246.374,
   "duration": 9.125,
   "narration": "In Kenya, keeping vultures away made carcasses last nearly three times longer, and tripled the number of mammals that came to feed.",
   "visual": {
    "type": "card",
