    "title": "Kenya, 2012",
    "rows": [
     [
      "Carcass lasts",
      "\u00d73"
     ],
     [
      "Mammal scavengers",
      "\u00d73"
     ]
    ],
    "tag": "STRONG",
    "map": "KEN"
   },
   "clip": "../09_Animation/SC033.mp4",
   "audio": "../10_Audio/narration/SC033.wav"
  },
  {
   "id": 34,
   "file": "SC034",
   "section": "A world without vultures",
   "start": 255.499,
   "duration": 4.458,
   "narration": "And in India, the mammal that showed up most was this one.",
   "visual": {
    "type": "plate",
    "shot": "P08",
    "move": "push"
   },
   "clip": "../09_Animation/SC034.mp4",
   "audio": "../10_Audio/narration/SC034.wav"
  },
  {
   "id": 35,
   "file": "SC035",
   "section": "A world without vultures",
   "start": 259.957,
   "duration": 8.708,
   "narration": "Week two. Stray dogs have found the dump. A meal that vultures would have finished in an afternoon is now a feast for the pack.",
   "visual": {
    "type": "plate",
    "shot": "P05",
    "move": "push",
    "tab": "WEEK 2",
    "fx": [
     "flies"
    ]
   },
   "clip": "../09_Animation/SC035.mp4",
   "audio": "../10_Audio/narration/SC035.wav"
  },
  {
   "id": 36,
   "file": "SC036",
   "section": "A world without vultures",
   "start": 268.665,
   "duration": 5.333,
   "narration": "More food means more puppies survive. By year one, the pack is bigger.",
   "visual": {
    "type": "plate",
    "shot": "P06",
    "move": "pan_l",
    "tab": "YEAR 1",
    "tag": "DEBATED"
   },
   "clip": "../09_Animation/SC036.mp4",
   "audio": "../10_Audio/narration/SC036.wav"
  },
  {
   "id": 37,
   "file": "SC037",
   "section": "A world without vultures",
   "start": 273.998,
   "duration": 11.083,
   "narration": "Across India, researchers saw feral dog numbers rise as the vultures vanished. Whether one caused the other is still debated, but the timing lines up.",
   "visual": {
    "type": "card",
    "card": "lines",
    "tag": "DEBATED"
   },
   "clip": "../09_Animation/SC037.mp4",
   "audio": "../10_Audio/narration/SC037.wav"
  },
  {
   "id": 38,
   "file": "SC038",
   "section": "A world without vultures",
   "start": 285.081,
   "duration": 4.5,
   "narration": "And dogs carry something vultures never spread: rabies.",
   "visual": {
    "type": "plate",
    "shot": "P18",
    "move": "push",
    "tab": "YEAR 1 \u00b7 The village"
   },
   "clip": "../09_Animation/SC038.mp4",
   "audio": "../10_Audio/narration/SC038.wav"
  },
  {
   "id": 39,
   "file": "SC039",
   "section": "A world without vultures",
   "start": 289.581,
   "duration": 8.167,
   "narration": "Dogs cause almost all human rabies cases, and India accounts for roughly a third of the world's rabies deaths.",
   "visual": {
